---
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { demoOnly } from "../../../lib/demo";
import { sampleNotice, webhookTypes } from "../../../sample/partner";

export const getStaticPaths = demoOnly;
---
<Base title="Live updates" description="How anySKU tells your site when something changes.">
  <div class="wrap section">
    <h1>Live updates</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Add your site's address on anySKU and choose what to hear about. Within about a minute of a change,
      anySKU sends your site a short notice, and your site decides what to do with it.
    </p>

    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Notice</th><th>Sent when</th><th>What your site might do</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {webhookTypes.map((w) => (
            <tr>
              <td><code>{w.type}</code></td>
              <td>{w.when}</td>
              <td>{w.idea}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <section class="month prose">
      <h2>What a notice looks like</h2>
      <pre><code>{JSON.stringify(sampleNotice, null, 2)}</code></pre>
      <p>
        A notice only says what changed and where. It never carries names, amounts or buyer details: your site
        looks those up with its key, so a notice that went astray reveals nothing.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Each notice is signed. Check the <code>AnySku-Signature</code> header before trusting it.</li>
        <li>Reply with any 2xx status. anySKU retries for about two days if your site is down, with the same <code>id</code>, so you can skip one you've already handled.</li>
        <li>Use <strong>Send test</strong> on the manage page to try your address.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Details and a signature example: <a href="https://www.anysku.com/developers/groups">anySKU for groups</a>.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
